{"id": "a212e389-704c-47df-b758-cfe568487a63", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll check this two ways. First, the Bedrock Knowledge Bases quotas that apply to your account and region, including Retrieve request rate and ingestion limits. Second, the actual throttling and usage signals, so we can see whether you're hitting a limit.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_oJEylTiCCzKT8sIi3vweQj", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "kb-quota-check", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["verifying-with-docs", "exploring-metrics", "searching-logs"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Determine whether Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases quotas explain (a) ThrottlingException on Retrieve calls under load and (b) slow ingestion jobs. Recommend concrete actions.",
  "context": "User reports their knowledge base ingestion is crawling and Retrieve (bedrock-agent-runtime) calls get ThrottlingException under load. They ask if they are hitting a quota and what to do. This is a bounded quota/limits check, not a root-cause hunt. Shallow pass.",
  "resources": ["Agent space account 123456789012, region us-east-1 (also check other regions with knowledge bases if none found there)", "Bedrock Knowledge Bases (bedrock-agent: list_knowledge_bases, list_data_sources, list_ingestion_jobs/get_ingestion_job)", "Service Quotas for service code 'bedrock'", "Vector store backing the KB (OpenSearch Serverless, Aurora, Pinecone, etc.) and the embedding model used"],
  "timeframe": "Last 24 hours up to 2026-11-17T18:46:00Z",
  "criteria": "1) Look up documented Bedrock KB quotas via docs (Retrieve / RetrieveAndGenerate requests per second, ingestion job limits: concurrent ingestion jobs, files/data per job, file size, StartIngestionJob rate) and note whether they are adjustable. 2) Use Service Quotas (list_service_quotas / get_service_quota for 'bedrock') to get this account's applied values for those quotas, and any quota-utilization data. 3) Look at the KB(s): list ingestion jobs with their durations, statistics (scanned/indexed/failed docs) and failure reasons; identify the embedding model and vector store, and check whether the embedding model's (e.g. Titan/Cohere) InvokeModel TPM/RPM quota or the vector store (OpenSearch Serverless OCU limits, Aurora capacity) is the more likely bottleneck for slow ingestion. 4) Check CloudWatch metrics (AWS/Bedrock invocation throttles, client errors, latency; OpenSearch Serverless metrics if relevant) for evidence of throttling. 5) Conclude: is a quota being hit (name which one and values), or is it something else? Give actionable recommendations (request quota increase via Service Quotas, client-side retries with exponential backoff and jitter, caching, reducing numResults/ batching, splitting data sources, scaling vector store, using provisioned throughput for the embedding model, etc.). Clearly separate verified facts from inference, and say if no KB or data was found."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Check Bedrock Knowledge Base quotas and throttling signals"}], "created_at": null}

